INT. SYNERGY DYNAMICS - OPEN OFFICE - DAY

Forty identical desks. Forty identical monitors. A banner reads WE ARE FAMILY!

DARRYL PENHALLOW, 30s, lanyard, tie two sizes too wide, stands bolt upright at his desk. Eyes wide. Smiling.

DARRYL (V.O.)
This is my third reorg this quarter. I've been promoted twice. I still do the same job.

He types. Fast. Frantic. Smiling.

DARRYL (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Synergy is not a word. It's a hostage note.

A cheerful intercom chime.

He grabs a stapler. Clutches it to his chest. Smiling.

DARRYL (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Quick wins. Low-hanging fruit. Circle back. Ping me.

He drops the stapler. Picks up a mug: WORLD'S OKAYEST EMPLOYEE.

DARRYL
(to the room, bright)
Great job, team!

No one answers. Forty monitors glow.

DARRYL (CONT'D)
(muttering)
We are so aligned.

He sips from the empty mug. Sets it down. Smiles.
